    not_duplicate_of: []  # 9190
    pr_ref:  # 9190
    description: "UAT 2026-04-13 BUG-14: `main()` calling `CliRunner().run(args)` resolves to the `CliRunner` class node rather than the `run` method. Forward slice does not traverse `contains` edges reached via a call, yielding 2 nodes (main + CliRunner class) instead of 19 nodes from slicing CliRunner directly. Fix: when call resolution lands on a class node, follow its `contains` edges to constructors/methods. Related to but distinct from WI-visaz (Kotlin extension call dispatch); see discussion note added there."  # 9190
    fields: {}  # 9190
- op: discuss  # 3a2e
  at: '2026-04-15T07:54:17Z'  # 3a2e
  by: agent  # 3a2e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3a2e
  clock: 2  # 3a2e
  nonce: 3a2e  # 3a2e
  message: "Investigated. The proposed fix (\"when call resolution lands on a class node, follow `contains` to constructors/methods\") collides head-on with `test_forward_slice_class_reaches_method_then_no_sibling_explosion` (test_slice.py:2295), which asserts the OPPOSITE: when a controller calls both `svc_create` and `service_class`, slice should reach `svc_create` but NOT `svc_delete`/`svc_list`. That test encodes an intentional design choice (slice.py:580–591) to prevent fan-out via shared ancestors.\n\nTwo possible reconciliations:\n\n**A. Precise heuristic (preserve both invariants).** Fan out from class node N reached via call from S only when S has NO other outgoing call edge to any method contained in N. Logic: \"S's intent toward N is unresolved → enumerate methods. S's intent is specific (resolved method on N already linked) → no fan-out.\" This satisfies both:\n- Existing test (2295): controller → svc_create AND controller → service_class. Controller has a resolved-method edge to a child of service_class, so no fan-out.\n- WI-gigoz: main → CliRunner only, no method edge from main to any CliRunner.* child. Fan out → reach run, init, etc.\n\nImplementation: at enqueue time for a class `next_node` reached from `current_id` via a call-like edge, check whether any other outgoing edge from `current_id` lands on a contains-child of `next_node`. If not, also enqueue the contains-children. ~30 lines in slice.py with a new test class; keeps existing tests green.\n\n**B. Structural fix at call resolution (true root cause).** The bug is upstream: `CliRunner().run(args)` should resolve `.run` to `CliRunner.run` and emit a calls edge to the method, not (only) to the class. Slice would then naturally include `run` via the direct edge. This is the \"Always structural\" path and would also fix every other place where chained `Class().method()` falls back to the class. Cost: per-language analyzer work in Java/Kotlin (and probably Python, JS, etc.). Substantially larger surface; needs a tracker item per language.\n\nRecommendation: do A first (gives users the slice they want now, doesn't regress the existing intent test) and open a sibling item for B as a structural follow-up. Path A's heuristic is also forward-compatible — once B lands and call resolution improves, A's \"fan out only when no resolved method\" rule naturally stops firing, so A doesn't accumulate as cruft.\n\nHolding implementation pending direction. If you'd rather skip A and go straight for B, I'll create the per-language structural-call-resolution items and pick one to start on."  # 3a2e
